Package: tux-guest
Version: 1.10.1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Tuxedo <tux@localhost>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: systemd, util-linux, cloud-guest-utils, gdisk, e2fsprogs, davfs2, python3, tzdata, python3-jeepney, nftables
Recommends: wl-clipboard, xclip, python3-cryptography, tux-va
Description: Tuxedo guest tools
 Grows the root partition and file system to the disk on every boot,
 does the one-time first-boot setup, mounts the shared folder at ~/Tux,
 shares the clipboard with the device on the desktop, follows the device's
 clock, time zone and screen brightness, tells the device when the
 focused program wants text, keeps windows above the device keyboard
 in Plasma, keeps the wallet (Secret Service and
 KWallet) in the device's Keychain, mounts the folders from the
 device's Files app at /media/tux, and adds the Tuxedo apt
 repository, off until it is turned on.
